1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
YouTube Playlist Player is a desktop app for viewing and reordering
the user's own YouTube playlists.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Step 1: The user clicks "Get my playlists".
The app opens the Google sign-in page in the browser.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The URL bar shows the OAuth client ID that is requesting access.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Step 2: The consent screen. The app requests the YouTube scope
(https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube).

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:38,000
It needs this scope to read the user's playlists and to change the order of
videos in a playlist. A read-only scope cannot do the second part.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The user reviews the request and clicks Allow.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Step 3: The app shows the user's playlists. Clicking a playlist expands it
and lists the videos it contains.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Step 4: Double-clicking a playlist opens a window where the user reorders
videos locally: sort by title, shuffle, or drag and drop.

9
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Nothing is sent to YouTube yet. All changes stay on the user's device.

10
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Step 5: The user clicks Push. The app shows how many playlist items
will be updated and asks for confirmation.

11
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:38,000
After confirmation, the app sends only the changes: playlistItems.update,
insert and delete, and playlists.insert for new playlists.

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Step 6: On youtube.com, the same playlist now shows the new order.

13
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The app never deletes playlists or uploads/deletes videos, and does not access
comments, subscriptions, or account settings.

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Data and sign-in tokens are stored only on the user's computer.
No data is sent to the developer's servers.
